gprofng: protect CALL_UTIL against glibc 2.43 function-like macros

glibc 2.43 defines strstr and similar functions as C23 _Generic macros.
CALL_UTIL(strstr) then expands to an unparsable member access. Parentheses
keep the member token from being expanded on rescan.

Backport of binutils commit 5f66aee7f4bec7a2d8378034116f5e5c3dc50f41
(Andreas Schwab).

diff -ru binutils-2.45.orig/gprofng/src/collector_module.h binutils-2.45/gprofng/src/collector_module.h
--- binutils-2.45.orig/gprofng/src/collector_module.h
+++ binutils-2.45/gprofng/src/collector_module.h
@@ -119,7 +119,7 @@ typedef struct CollectorUtilFuncs
 extern CollectorUtilFuncs __collector_util_funcs;
 extern int __collector_dlsym_guard;
 
-#define CALL_UTIL(x) __collector_util_funcs.x
+#define CALL_UTIL(x) (__collector_util_funcs.x)
 
 /* The following constants define the meaning of the "void *arg"
  * argument of getFrameInfo().
